<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} head={head}>
<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>Mortgage Refinance in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Refinance options</p><h1>Mortgage Refinance in Miami</h1><p>Compare refinance options for Miami homeowners, including rate-and-term, cash-out, FHA, VA, conventional, and jumbo structures.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Review Refinance Options</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Estimate Payment</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>A refinance can be used to adjust your mortgage structure, access equity, remove or change mortgage insurance, consolidate debts, or compare current financing options. The right choice depends on your goals and total cost over time.</p><p>Because mortgage rates change frequently, a refinance review should compare monthly payment, closing costs, break-even period, cash out, taxes, insurance, and loan term.</p><h2>Rate-and-term refinance</h2><p>A rate-and-term refinance is often used to change the rate, payment, or loan term without taking substantial cash out. The analysis should include closing costs and how long you plan to keep the loan.</p><p>A lower payment is not always the only goal; term length and total interest matter too.</p><h2>Cash-out refinance</h2><p>A cash-out refinance may allow qualified homeowners to access equity for renovations, debt consolidation, investment, reserves, or other financial goals. Equity, credit, income, property type, and loan-to-value matter.</p><p>For condos, building documentation and insurance may still be part of the review.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a Mortgage Refinance Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Mortgage Refinance in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>When does refinancing make sense?</summary><p>It depends on your current loan, new loan terms, costs, break-even point, equity, credit, and goals. A personalized comparison is needed.</p></details><details><summary>Can I refinance a Miami condo?</summary><p>Yes, but the condo building may still need to meet lender requirements.</p></details><details><summary>Is cash-out refinancing available in Florida?</summary><p>Cash-out refinance options may be available for qualified homeowners, depending on equity, occupancy, credit, income, and property type.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="cash-out-refinance-miami.html">Cash-Out Refinance Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="miami-mortgage-rates.html">Miami Mortgage Rates<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Mortgage Calculator Florida<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="jumbo-loans-miami.html">Jumbo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a></div>